WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.750
“Has Luffy grown as a leader over the course
of the story?”

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.049
That is what I was originally planning on
talking about in this video.

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:10.059
And we WILL actually also answer this question
later on.

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:14.400
But while doing the research on Luffy´s development
as the leader of the straw-hats, I very quickly

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.180
became aware of a simple truth: Luffy is,
and always has been a great leader.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.110
Now this obviously does not mean that Luffy
doesn´t have any flaws or room for improvement

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.710
in his role as a captain.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:28.320
And we will also discuss that towards the
end of this video, but it much rather means

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.420
that Luffy as a person fulfills a TON of requirements
that make up a good leader.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.960
Leadership is an essential part of our world
and therefore, it is often at the center of

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.579
much attention and debate.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:42.960
At its core, a leader is simply the person
holding the most power in a group or organization

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.260
of people.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.530
Leadership by itself is therefore actually
a very neutral term.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.150
As a result, you will probably not have a
single person in mind when you hear the term

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.150
leader.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.400
Rather you will think of good leaders and
evil leaders, of cruel leaders and kind leaders

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.620
and of inspiring leaders and ineffective leaders,
as well as many more.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.920
But why is it that we look up to some of these
people while we dislike others?

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.920
Why do we like some evil characters better
than good ones?

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.670
And what actually makes a great Leader?

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.020
Let´s take a look.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.280
There are many elements and aspects that determine
how leadership plays out.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.429
But in the end, it all comes down to the person
itself.

00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:23.009
This combination of individual personality
and power makes leadership a concept that

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:27.220
fascinates us and that therefore plays a key
role in many stories.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.369
One Piece is no exception for this.

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:33.409
The One Piece world is filled with different
kinds of Organizations with different kind

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:34.490
of ideologies.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.810
The different leaders of the marines have
different values and goals.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.039
The different pirate captains have individual
leadership styles and ambitions.

00:01:42.039 --> 00:01:43.039
And every.

00:01:43.039 --> 00:01:44.039
Character.

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:47.210
became a leader under different circumstances
and for different reasons.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.030
This makes it so incredibly fascinating for
us to watch opposed groups clash with each

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.560
other in the story.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.259
No two leaders are the same.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:58.659
In the context of One Piece this diversity
of leadership styles, that Oda introduced,

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:03.069
is what manages to give the huge number of
characters and groups in the world individual

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:05.459
and memorable features and themes.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:09.400
Because at the bottom of it, every marine
or pirate crew mirrors the leadership style

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.400
of their captain.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.909
But, while there are countless leaders in
One Piece that might be worth talking about,

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:18.220
today we will discuss the most important of
them all: The leader of the straw-hat pirates:

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.220
Monkey D. Luffy.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:23.390
As I have mentioned already, I´d like to
argue that amid all the criticism of Luffy´s

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.659
leadership style and character, he has actually
always been a great leader with the potential

00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:29.170
to become even better.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:33.079
As a basis for this argument I´d like to
discuss the different characteristics and

00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:37.590
personality traits that are associated with
good leadership and then compare them with

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.590
Luffy´s character.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:42.849
So, let´s start with the 6 most commonly
stated personality traits that can be found

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:47.299
in great leaders:
The first trait we look at here, is honesty.

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:51.020
Honesty is an important personality trait
for leaders because it inspires trust and

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.840
credibility within their followers.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:56.970
This again brings with it many positive factors
when it comes to teamwork.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:00.060
As we all know, Luffy is an honest person
through and through.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.480
He is more or less incapable of lying and
probably has one of the worst pokerfaced in

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.480
history.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.719
While this can sometimes come across as annoying
or tactless in the story, it is the bases

00:03:09.719 --> 00:03:13.390
of why the crew trusts him so much and takes
his words seriously.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:16.439
The second important leadership trait is a
sense of humor.

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:21.319
This not only makes the leader more likeable,
but also creates a friendly and positive atmosphere

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:22.319
in the group.

00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:26.719
Luffy´s sense of humor and the lightheartedness
that comes with it is the reason that the

00:03:26.719 --> 00:03:30.360
Straw-hat Pirates are so very different from
any other pirate crew you could come across

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.189
in the grand line, with the exception of shanks
maybe.

00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:37.390
The crew feels comfortable and respected and
are able to form bonds on a level that goes

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:39.680
far beyond what most other crews have.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.079
An example for this would be Luffy´s imitation
of his crewmates.

00:03:44.079 --> 00:03:47.010
Next on, we have confidence.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:51.540
While confidence is a great trait for a leader
in many aspects, the most important one is

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.459
inspiring motivation among the group.

00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:58.909
Luffy´s confidence is pretty much beyond
limits and is a central part of his character.

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:03.689
No matter how bad the situation, he is confident
in his ability to overcome any hardship with

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:04.769
his powers.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:06.370
Just look at the fight with Katakuri.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:10.659
Additionally, he is also confident in the
characters and powers of each and every one

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:14.650
of his crewmates, which might be perceived
as naïve, but ends up creating even more

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.580
trust and loyalty towards him.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:22.330
This could be seen with Sanji in Whole Cake
Island or Robin in the Enis Lobby arc.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.630
Connected to the previous two, the 5th important
leadership trait is having a positive attitude.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.640
Approaching challenges and hardships with
a positive perspective is important in order

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.170
to enable your group to create the necessary
conviction and motivation to tackle these

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:37.170
challenges.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.540
Luffy without a doubt shares also this personality
trait.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.300
And that to the extent that he took on the
plan to take down Kaido with a broad grin,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.860
while Law was clearly being more serious and
pessimistic about it.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.611
Still I think you could argue that without
Luffy´s positive attitude, the Straw hats

00:04:51.611 --> 00:04:54.110
might never have made it to where they are
now.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:57.910
Last but not least, the 6th central leadership
trait is creativity.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.840
This trait is important to find creative and
flexible solutions to unexpected problems.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.840
Now while Luffy is in no means a genius when
it comes to creating creative strategies,

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.190
he definitely proved to be creative when it
comes to fighting.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:14.590
His creativity can especially be seen in the
way he uses his devil fruit in more than creative

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.590
ways.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.130
Simply the way that his gear system works,
is more than creative by itself.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:23.870
Additionally, the way he has built his crew
can definitely also be described as creative.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:27.480
Now, just to make it clear, I have not made
up any of these factors.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:30.380
I have taken them from up-to-date research
on leadership.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.910
And yet Luffy shares all of these traits to
a certain extend.

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:36.000
I do not believe that this a coincidence.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.430
I rather think that Oda constructed Luffy´s
character exactly in this manner to make him

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.430
as likable and able as possible as the leader
of the straw-hat pirates and the main character

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:45.430
of the story.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:49.470
To prove this even more, let´s look at the
5 most important principles of a great leader

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:53.960
and weather Luffy shares them as well:
The first principle we´re gonna look at is

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.720
“leading by example”.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:00.030
In other words: It is important to be able
to do yourself what you expect your followers

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.180
to do.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:03.750
This is pretty much Luffy´s supreme discipline.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.250
Luffy always goes first heads on into the
fight.

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.210
He does not expect his crew to do his job,
but rather sees it as his duty to fight and

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.230
bleed for them.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:15.270
A good example for this his fight against
Katakuri that Luffy only starts and enters

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:17.950
on his own, to allow his crew to get away.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.490
The second principle is “talk less, listen
more”.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.570
While many leaders think it is important to
do all the talking and demonstrate skill,

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:29.930
it is actually much better to involve the
group into discussions and decisions.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.870
This is especially important to get people
on your side and connect with you.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.990
In return it shows your respect for your group
members.

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.630
As we know, Luffy is defiantly not the super
talkative guy.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:44.450
When it comes to making decisions or even
to fighting, everyone in the crew can have

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.450
their say in it.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.640
Tactics and tasks are decided on together.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.370
This creates a sense of equality and respect
in the Straw hat crew.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.650
Next, it is important to “not play favorites”.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.991
While this one should be quite obvious, in
many groups in the One piece world, certain

00:06:57.991 --> 00:07:01.090
people receive special treatment or status.

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:05.850
Luffy however has never given any straw hat
a different treatment than any of the others.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:09.510
This strengthens his credibility and respect
within the crew.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.550
The fourth principle we´re looking at is
“be yourself”.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:17.220
This one is, once again, very important for
credibility and authenticity which will strengthen

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.710
the morale in the group.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:22.570
This principle is actually much more prominent
in the One Piece world than in ours.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:26.180
While many leaders in our society definitely
“aren´t themselves” in a way, in the

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.910
context of One Piece, only Buggy comes to
mind when it comes to breaking this principle.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:35.180
Now the last important leadership principle
is “taking responsibility for your actions”.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:40.580
In essence this means two things: Sharing
success with the group and taking the blame

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.860
when something goes wrong.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:46.170
Luffy does not only take the responsibility
for his own actions, but also takes the blame

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.900
of others to protect them.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.840
For example, when Big Mom threatened to destroy
Fish-Man Island for not supplying her with

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.330
their monthly candy tribute, Luffy took the
blame of eating all of the candy to protect

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.740
the island from Big Mom's wrath.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:02.530
Also, when Katakuri apologized to Luffy for
Flampe interfering with their fight, Luffy

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:06.310
told him that fighting dirty is normal in
a battle between pirates, and that it was

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:09.460
his mistake for not dodging.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:14.180
What has become very clear in my mind is that
Luffy actually fulfills all of the most important

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.270
personality traits and principles that a great
leader needs to succeed.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:22.840
He inspires and motivates his Nakama and he
has built a crew that is as loyal and close

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:25.430
as maybe no other in One Piece.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:29.870
So now, this leads me directly to the question
of why so many people think that Luffy is

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:33.000
not a good enough leader at this point in
the story.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.140
And the only way I can rationalize this is
that people have expectations towards Luffy

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:39.610
that he simply cannot fulfill.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:43.780
People seem to yearn for a more “badass”
leadership style from Luffy and I often see

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:45.490
the comparison to Law.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:50.060
Not only is Luffy a great leader the way he
is, but also becoming more serious or stern

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:54.070
would lead to Luffy´s personality getting
lost resulting in a character that has little

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.130
to do with the Luffy we love.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:09:00.300
Additionally, without the positive and careless
approach that characterizes Luffy´s leadership

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.810
style it is not clear that the Straw Hats
would succeed in the New World.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.870
Luck and positive will play a huge role in
the crew’s success.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:12.030
Another point of criticism that I often hear
is that Luffy hasn´t really developed as

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.070
a leader over time.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.730
I also think that this is only true partially,
if at all.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:21.040
The time skip, but especially Whole Cake Island
have shown that Luffy has in fact lost some

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.430
of his naivete and has grown.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:28.450
This can be seen in various instances: Luffy
stayed calm after Pedro was killed and he

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:31.890
saw sense in and supported the plan to bring
down Big Mom.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:36.740
Luffy also started fighting smarter: He mostly
avoided a direct confrontation with Big Mom

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:40.650
and accepted the power difference between
himself and Katakuri.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:45.600
And he also used Bruleé to move around more
freely while recharging his Haki.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.290
All of these behaviors we most likely wouldn´t
have seen from pre-time skip Luffy.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:54.770
Now having said that, I certainly DO think
that there is an area that Luffy can and maybe

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.320
should improve in.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.760
And that is leadership skills.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.700
While Luffy has a great set of personality
traits and principles that make him a great

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:06.510
leader, there are many skills that make leadership
more effective and that might be necessary

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:08.030
to make it to Raftel in the end.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:11.670
While there are probably a few skills that
might be necessary for Luffy to learn in terms

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:16.240
of leading his crew, I want to introduce two
that I find particularly important: “Thinking

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.530
ahead” and “creating a strategy”.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:22.950
While I don´t think that Luffy needs to become
more serious in order to become cooler (because

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:27.950
let´s face it, Luffy is already super cool!),
I DO think that he should think ahead a little

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:29.300
more from time to time.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:33.760
And even though Luffy is not famous for great
acts of thinking, he certainly isn´t stupid.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:37.680
So I think that this would definitely be a
skill that he would be able to learn and that

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:41.270
would prove immensely useful the closer he
gets to become the pirate king.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.800
Now the second skill builds a little bit on
top of the first.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:49.000
After thinking ahead, it would be smart to
use the insight you get and translate them

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.250
into a useful plan or strategy.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:54.920
Same as with the previous point, I think that
Luffy would be more than capable of doing

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.480
so, even if it might act out in a different
way than we would expect.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:04.020
So all in all, based on the arguments of leadership
personality traits, principles and skills,

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:10.050
I hope I could lay out for you why I think
that Luffy is actually a great leader.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:13.360
If you made it this far into the video, I
am sure you have your own thoughts about this

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.360
topic!

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.110
So, please let me know your opinion in the
comments below.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.650
Do you think Luffy is a good leader?

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:22.920
Do you think there are other important leadership
traits that Luffy has or does not have?

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.040
And where do you think Luffy still needs to
grow in the future?

